#EMBEDDED_NOTES
#A D-Class Sedan with Motion Sensors drives on a Cross Slope Sine Sweep road.
#
#The 5 Motion Sensors all are attached the vehicle's Sprung Mass and Sprung Mass wheel height position. This example is to show difference between sensors on sprung mass and unsprung mass.
#
#The Cross Slope Sine Sweep road data varies in both frequency and amplitude, exciting various bounce, pitch, and roll motions of the vehicle.
#
#END_EMBEDDED_NOTES

